WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.240
It’s project time, and today you are a party planner with two thousand rupees to spend!

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.790
You have ₹2,000 to plan a birthday party for ten friends.

3
00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:14.320
You must keep at least ₹200 as savings.

4
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.460
Your plan must cover the must-haves before any nice-to-haves.

5
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.260
Must-haves are the things the party cannot happen without.

6
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:28.420
For our party, they are a cake, snacks, drinks and simple decorations.

7
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.810
Price these first and add them up.

8
00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:37.910
Nice-to-haves make the party extra fun, like return gifts, a magician or a music speaker.

9
00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.220
Choose them only with the money left after the must-haves and savings.

10
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.750
You cannot have them all, so pick your favourites.

11
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.370
Show your plan to the class like a real party planner.

12
00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:53.830
Say your total, your savings and one hard choice you made.

13
00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.320
Explain what you gave up and why.

14
00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:01.860
Our party budget is two thousand rupees, and we will keep two hundred rupees as savings.

15
00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:07.480
The cake, snacks, drinks and decorations add up to one thousand three hundred rupees.

16
00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:13.990
Two thousand minus one thousand three hundred is seven hundred rupees.

17
00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:19.690
Take away the two hundred rupees of savings, and five hundred rupees is left for nice-to-haves.

18
00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:26.670
Meera really wants a magician, but the magician costs eight hundred rupees.

19
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:32.310
That is more than the five hundred rupees she has for nice-to-haves.

20
00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:38.380
Return gifts and party hats together cost four hundred rupees, and they fit.

21
00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:44.590
Meera chooses the return gifts and hats, and she says what she gave up when she presents.

22
00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.130
A great presentation shows every item and its price, so anyone can check your maths.

23
00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:53.090
Say your total spending and how much you saved.

24
00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:56.280
Then share one hard choice, and what you gave up to make it.

25
00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:03.470
Speak slowly and clearly, and smile, because you are the party planner today.

26
00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:06.570
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

27
00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.370
Now plan it, build it, test it, and share it!
